<title>NETHERLANDS: Nedlloyd sells stake in Brink's venture.</title>
<headline>Nedlloyd sells stake in Brink's venture.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipping and road transport group Koninklijke Nedlloyd NV said on Monday it intends to sell its 35 percent stake in Brink's Nedlloyd to Brink's Security International, making the U.S. company the sole owner of the Dutch valuables transport firm.</p>
<p>Brink's Nedlloyd's activities have not been considered to be part of Nedlloyd's core activities for quite a while, Nedlloyd said. It sold 65 percent of the unit to Brink's in 1988.</p>
<p>Brink's Nedlloyd has 650 employees. No financial details of the intended sale were disclosed.</p>
